{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01QKMEW5o1VzjAVvJnf7bT7h", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/2968\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hac.bard.edu/amor-mundi/roth-and-arendt-together-for-eternity-2018-05-27\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hac.bard.edu/walk-to-hannah-arendts-grave\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.bard.edu/inside/calendar/commemorating-hannah-arendt-december-4-1975\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.heyalma.com/why-i-traveled-100-miles-to-visit-hannah-arendts-grave/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hac.bard.edu/event/index.php?eid=151377\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.bard.edu/inside/calendar/hannah-arendt-walking-tour\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hac.bard.edu/amor-mundi/tekhines-2024-03-31\"}, {\"url\": \"https://beta.empireadc.org/search/catalog/nanb_5342\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:01:45.892Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Hannah Arendt buried Bard College Leon Botstein longest-serving president", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01SgcEWYSAUJaSgxDTDzMsfw", "content": [{"title": "www.findagrave.com", "url": "https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/2968"}, {"title": "roth and arendt together for eternity 2018 05 27", "url": "https://hac.bard.edu/amor-mundi/roth-and-arendt-together-for-eternity-2018-05-27"}, {"title": "walk to hannah arendts grave", "url": "https://hac.bard.edu/walk-to-hannah-arendts-grave"}, {"title": "commemorating hannah arendt december 4 1975", "url": "https://www.bard.edu/inside/calendar/commemorating-hannah-arendt-december-4-1975"}, {"title": "Why I Traveled 100 Miles To Visit Hannah Arendt’s Grave", "url": "https://www.heyalma.com/why-i-traveled-100-miles-to-visit-hannah-arendts-grave/"}, {"title": "hac.bard.edu", "url": "https://hac.bard.edu/event/index.php?eid=151377"}, {"title": "hannah arendt walking tour", "url": "https://www.bard.edu/inside/calendar/hannah-arendt-walking-tour"}, {"title": "tekhines 2024 03 31", "url": "https://hac.bard.edu/amor-mundi/tekhines-2024-03-31"}, {"title": "Hannah Arendt Ephemera Collection, ca. 1950-2006, bulk ca. 1950-1976", "url": "https://beta.empireadc.org/search/catalog/nanb_5342"}]}, "The search confirms Arendt's burial at Bard, but it doesn't address Botstein's tenure.\n\n- **Burial site:** Arendt is buried in the Bard College cemetery, alongside her husband Heinrich Blücher, who taught at Bard. She is buried alongside Blücher in the Bard College Cemetery. A Find a Grave entry also lists the Bard College Cemetery in Annandale-on-Hudson, New York. Find a Grave memorial ID 2968 cites Bard College Cemetery, Annandale-on-Hudson, Dutchess County, New York.\n- **Botstein's connection:** The Bard HAC's Roth and Arendt post quotes Botstein's account of why Philip Roth chose burial there. According to an anecdote related by Bard's President, Leon Botstein, Roth requested to be buried in the Bard cemetery so that he would be able to talk to his friend and Bard faculty member Norman Manea. That is the only Botstein reference in the results.\n- **Longest-serving claim:** Nothing in the results says whether Botstein is Bard's longest-serving president. That claim is unverified here."], "durationSeconds": 5.807451833000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01QKMEW5o1VzjAVvJnf7bT7h", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
