{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_013fWCsL6di24nnZV5qSuyfq", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon_Botstein\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.iwm.at/fellow/leon-botstein\"}, {\"url\": \"https://fulbright.edu.vn/?p=51993\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ci.digitellinc.com/b/sp/leon-botstein-274\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hedgehogreview.com/contributors/leon-botstein\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ijn.com/?p=535232\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ijn.com/leon-botstein-heritage-forgotten-people-music-bard/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://brockinstitute.org/nominee/leon-botstein\"}, {\"url\": \"https://brockinstitute.org/nominee-leon-botstein\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:01:53.278Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Leon Botstein president of Bard College since 1975", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_019r1iDqQKA96aXGscoZPs2T", "content": [{"title": "Leon Botstein", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon_Botstein"}, {"title": "Leon Botstein", "url": "https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon Botstein"}, {"title": "leon botstein", "url": "https://www.iwm.at/fellow/leon-botstein"}, {"title": "fulbright.edu.vn", "url": "https://fulbright.edu.vn/?p=51993"}, {"title": "leon botstein 274", "url": "https://ci.digitellinc.com/b/sp/leon-botstein-274"}, {"title": "Leon Botstein", "url": "https://hedgehogreview.com/contributors/leon-botstein"}, {"title": "By Shira Li Bartov", "url": "https://www.ijn.com/?p=535232"}, {"title": "By Shira Li Bartov", "url": "https://www.ijn.com/leon-botstein-heritage-forgotten-people-music-bard/"}, {"title": "President of Bard College", "url": "https://brockinstitute.org/nominee/leon-botstein"}, {"title": "Leon Botstein", "url": "https://brockinstitute.org/nominee-leon-botstein"}]}, "The search confirms the 1975 start date, but the most recent source says he is no longer president, and several older pages still describe him as current.\n\n- **Start date:** Multiple sources agree he took over Bard in 1975. One says he left Franconia to become the president of Bard College that year, after earlier leading Franconia College in New Hampshire.\n- **Tenure:** Wikipedia lists his term as 1975–2026, with Jonathan Becker as acting successor. It reports that his retirement from the presidency in June 2026 was shaped by revelations about his past relationship with Jeffrey Epstein.\n- **Later departure:** The same article says that in October 2026, he resigned from his remaining roles at Bard College, including his professorship and his conducting post.\n- **Outdated pages:** Several bios (IWM, Brock Institute, Hedgehog Review) still describe him as current president. They appear to predate his retirement."], "durationSeconds": 4.9670799589999985, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_013fWCsL6di24nnZV5qSuyfq", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
